# Build context for tds-gateway-api's `frontends` compose profile, which runs
# this product's packed release/ tree in a container
# (tds-gateway-api/deploy/Dockerfile.frontend).
#
# Two of these lines are not housekeeping:
#
#   **/node_modules  Two trees match — the development one at the root and the
#                    packed one inside release/, ~170 MB. Both are installed
#                    FOR THE DEVELOPER'S MACHINE; on Windows they hold win32
#                    binaries (sharp most visibly) that Linux cannot load. The
#                    image reinstalls from release/package.json, which lists
#                    only public packages, so a copied tree is both useless and
#                    the largest single thing in the transfer.
#
#   .env             A local developer .env would otherwise be baked into an
#                    image layer. Nothing in the container reads one: every
#                    PUBLIC_* value is already compiled into release/ by the
#                    build that produced it.
**/node_modules
.env
.env.production

.git
.github
.astro
dist
var
*.log
